    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.86). **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear top play, benefiting from a favorable 4.78 xERA matchup against Bailey Ober and a significant situational boost due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which projects a 92% steal opportunity\u2014a critical metric for our scarcity-focused build. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** finds himself in an ideal spot against the lefty Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez; he carries a strong platoon edge (+14%) and the necessary speed profile to potentially shift the needle in the stolen base category. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) also remains a pillar of our lineup today, as he draws a +7% platoon advantage against Patrick Sandoval.\n\nWhile the core of the lineup is set, the bench decision regarding **Jackson Merrill** (39.03) was the most difficult. Despite his talent, the combination of a tough matchup against Kyle Harrison (2.92 xERA) and a significant -13% penalty for the platoon disadvantage pushed him just below our \"Marginal\" start threshold. Consequently, we are prioritizing the higher output of **Kyle Tucker** (71.17) and **Andy Pages** (65.78), who both enjoy better situational park and skill-based projections. We are also keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Sam Antonacci**; as their official lineups remain pending, we are assuming their positions based on recent trends. Should those orders shift significantly, we may need to adjust our aggression, particularly with **Coby Mayo** (53.68), whose -8% platoon risk against Bailey Ober leaves him on the lower end of our starting efficiency spectrum.",
